nticated\n  using (owner = (select auth.uid()) and deleted_at is null)\n  with check (owner = (select auth.uid()) and deleted_at is null);\n\n-- No delete policy and no DELETE privilege: hard deletes are impossible via the app.\n\ncreate function public.soft_delete(entry_id uuid)\nreturns void\nlanguage plpgsql\nsecurity definer\nset search_path = ''\nas $$\ndeclare\n  caller uuid := auth.uid();\nbegin\n  if caller is null then\n    raise exception 'not authenticated' using errcode = '28000';\n  end if;\n\n  update public.entry\n     set deleted_at = now()\n   where id = entry_id\n     and owner = caller\n     and deleted_at is null;\n\n  if not found then\n    raise exception 'entry not found or not owned by caller' using errcode = '42501';\n  end if;\nend;\n$$;\n\nrevoke all on function public.soft_delete(uuid) from public, anon;\ngrant execute on function public.soft_delete(uuid) to authenticated;\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018h2bATGyFS3qkGcePfuDiN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8uDeNXey62cerKtsQP5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the schema to `supabase/migrations/20261117000000_journal_entries.sql`. I haven't run it against a database.\n\n- **Table:** `entry` has the columns from your contract. `owner` defaults to `auth.uid()`. Row-level security is on.\n- **Visibility:** the select policy shows a user only their own entries where `deleted_at` is null. A deleted entry is hidden from its owner too, and no app role can read it.\n- **Create and edit:** a user can insert entries for themselves and edit the `body` of their own live entries. They can't change `owner` or set `deleted_at` directly.\n- **No hard delete:** `authenticated` has no `DELETE` privilege and there is no delete policy, so the app can't remove a row. A user also can't clear `deleted_at`, because the entry is hidden from them and they can't write that column. Recovery is left to an administrator working directly on the database.\n- **`soft_delete(entry_id uuid)`:** it sets `deleted_at = now()` on the caller's own live entry. It raises an error if the caller isn't signed in, or if the entry doesn't exist, isn't theirs, or is already deleted. Only `authenticated` can call it, and the table is only touched through it.\n\nBecause only `owner` and `body` are insertable, a test that supplies its own `id` on insert would fail. I assumed `id` is always generated."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1727,"cache_read_input_tokens":32434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1727},"output_tokens":454,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9209896-ce6c-4aef-9b5c-4afc1a37c5e9","uuid":"423bef